{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And you shall make upon the breastpiece — upon its two upper ends you place the rings, to insert into them the two cords, and you place their two ends that are set in the settings upon the shoulder-pieces of the ephod, and so the breastpiece hangs from the ephod. Yet the bottom edge of the breastpiece can still sway this way and that, until they attach it to the ephod, as I proceed to explain: he makes at the ends of the breastpiece, on the inside, two rings, one here and one there, and two rings at the ends of the ephod, at the bottom of the shoulder-pieces, at the place where they join from below to the ephod, and the band from above. And those of the breastpiece are below and those of the ephod are above, and when a tekhelet cord comes from the rings of the ephod to the rings of the breastpiece, [the breastpiece] is above and the ephod is below."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The bracketed [החשן] in the last sentence reflects a correction in the Hebrew text; the syntax is strained and the antecedent of 'is above/is below' is textually uncertain. I have translated hyper-literally without resolving the difficulty."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:29.259084163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}